<p>European Union foreign ministers agreed Monday to impose new sanctions on Israeli settlers accused of violence against Palestinians in the occupied West Bank and on senior Hamas figures, EU foreign policy chief Kaja Kallas said after talks in Brussels. The settler package targets three people and four settler organisations whose names had not yet been published, while Ynet reported that the Hamas measures cover 10 senior officials. The agreement followed months of opposition from Hungary’s previous government and moved ahead after Hungary’s new government dropped its veto, according to European reports and officials. The EU stopped short of broader economic measures against Israel, including stronger trade pressure or suspension of the EU-Israel association framework, despite calls from some European governments. Israel denounced the decision as political and rejected what it called a false comparison between Israeli citizens and Hamas.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/XPd8PUHb0x9fMpsiCKdzXJ-_DynGjD7k2vVXtfb07z6hpugDKzvN5LcrC03RUZo9QX25DQ-pgsLVFwaSn0Z_KYJ9tlg6ivdUrvL5wEX3ShBfLfCBaXbC6LlcrUyThegs-dZz-7FUw6z2a8noRImw26YbcRiLoLXWU5BIGZa9YQawkxJ5V9fnd93nT0BpZ5lyiP_fBU0plHUJXl0tMhMkVUOtjrs' alt='Israeli settlers blocking a road as they try to stop Palestinian farmers from leaving their land after harvesting their olive trees in the village of Silwad, near East Ramallah, in October.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Proposal origin: Avvenire reported that the settler-sanctions proposal dated to September.</li><li>EU proponents: Avvenire reported that Ireland, Slovenia and Spain had pushed for the settler sanctions in a letter.</li><li>Hamas response: Dawn reported no immediate response from Hamas after the EU announcement.</li><li>Scope criticism: The Guardian reported that one MEP called the move a “baby step”.</li></ul><blockquote>It was high time we move from deadlock to delivery - Kaja Kallas</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>European Union: Kaja Kallas said ministers had approved sanctions and that the EU was applying consequences for extremism and violence. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1999449/eu-ministers-agree-on-sanctions-targeting-violent-west-bank-settlers'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Israel: Foreign Minister Gideon Sa’ar said the EU had targeted Israeli citizens and entities because of political views and objected to including Israeli citizens and Hamas members in the same sanctions announcement. (<a href='https://www.ynetnews.com/article/h1t0hdjyml'>Ynet</a>)</li><li>Israeli prime minister’s office: The prime minister’s office said on X that Israel and the United States were “doing Europe’s dirty work” by fighting jihadist groups in Iran and elsewhere. (<a href='https://tribune.com.pk/story/2607611/eu-agrees-sanctions-on-israeli-settlers'>Tribune</a>)</li><li>France: Foreign Minister Jean-Noël Barrot said the EU was sanctioning major Israeli organisations accused of supporting extremist and violent colonisation of the West Bank, while also adopting measures against Hamas leaders. (<a href='https://www.middleeastmonitor.com/20260511-eu-agrees-on-sanctions-targeting-israeli-occupiers-in-west-bank/'>Middle East Monitor</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://japantoday.com/category/world/eu-sanctions-hamas-leaders-and-israeli-settlers-but-shelves-stronger-economic-pressure'>EU diplomats agree to sanction Hamas leaders and Israeli settlers but fail to pressure Israel</a> - japantoday.com</li><li><a href='https://www.npr.org/2026/05/12/g-s1-121581/eu-sanction-hamas-leaders-israeli-settlers'>EU diplomats agree to sanction Hamas leaders and Israeli settlers</a> - npr.org</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/eu-greenlights-sanctions-on-israeli-west-bank-settlers/a-77123631'>EU greenlights sanctions on Israeli West Bank settlers</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/eu-agrees-sanctions-on-west-bank-settlers-and-hamas-leaders/article70967301.ece'>EU agrees san